Z||000006||87GTZ34||03-14-2001||09:31 PM||||Alex, More than likely the oil is being drawn in thru the crank vent system and settling into the egr tube (gravity).  Look at the path from the tube on the intake to the egr and see if there is an oil trail.<P>think horses not zebras?!?<p>[This message has been edited by 87GTZ34 (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||03-14-2001||09:37 PM||||Ron, I guess that's the case. There is a low point in the tube lower than both tube ends. Also because my chip does not activate the EGR I guess it doesn't get burned also. I may plug it later on. Just painted the EGR valve assy and looks to good to eliminate  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||87GTZ34||03-14-2001||10:47 PM||||Check the PCV valve and make sure you're not getting air constantly sucking thru the crankcase.  At the very least the valve should rattle but it doesn't guarantee that it is sealing when it should. If in doubt replace it, I think they're only about 3 bucks.||||reg||1
